## Working agreement

- `/workspace` is the PR's own branch. Make your changes directly there — they
  will be pushed back to this PR.
- You may run any commands you need — build, tests, linters, package managers.
  This container is your sandbox.
- Network access is available and you run as root: install whatever the project
  needs (`uv`, `pip`, `npm`/`pnpm`/`yarn`, or system packages via `apt-get`).
  Node and Python 3 (with `uv`) are preinstalled.
- Do not touch git history or remotes. The host commits and pushes after you
  finish.

## What to do

Advance the pull request: implement requested changes, fix problems, and finish
the work described above. Keep changes focused and consistent with the existing
code and the PR's intent.

## Definition of Done

1. The work is implemented, focused, and consistent with the PR.
2. Add or update tests where appropriate, and run the project's checks where you
   can.
3. Write a concise summary of what you changed to `/workspace/AGENT_RESULT.md`.
4. Write a clear commit message (one-line subject + body) to
   `/workspace/COMMIT_MSG.md`.

## Summary style (important)

Write `AGENT_RESULT.md` as a normal PR update comment in plain, neutral voice.
Do **not** refer to yourself as an AI, an agent, an assistant, or mention that
the work was automated. Just describe what changed.

